---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Alexis Thomas"
  description="How alexisthomas.fr handles your data: analytics cookies and your choice, error reports, and the contact form."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy" }]}
>
  <article class="privacy wrap">
    <p class="label">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="hl title">Privacy</h1>
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        This is my personal website. It has no accounts and no ads, and I never sell or share your data. This page
        covers the website only; the Aura app has its own <a href="/aura/privacypolicy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        I use Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages are read, including downloads of my CV and
        sent contact messages (never what they say). It sets first-party cookies, and Google processes the data on
        my behalf. In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, analytics cookies stay off
        until you accept them in the banner; elsewhere they are on by default. Advertising storage, ad
        personalization and ad user data are always off.
      </p>
      <p class="choice" data-choice>
        <span data-choice-text>Your choice is kept in this browser.</span>
        <button type="button" data-set="granted">Allow analytics</button>
        <button type="button" data-set="denied" class="ghost">Turn off analytics</button>
      </p>

      <h2>Error reports</h2>
      <p>
        When something breaks on a page, an error report (the error, the page address, and the browser and device
        type) goes to Sentry so I can fix it. It sets no cookies and includes no name or email.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact form</h2>
      <p>
        Messages sent through the contact form (your name, email and message) are emailed to me and used only to
        reply to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:contact@alexisthomas.fr">contact@alexisthomas.fr</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var text = document.querySelector("[data-choice-text]");
    function show() {
      var c = null;
      try {
        c = localStorage.getItem("consent");
      } catch (e) {}
      text.textContent =
        c === "granted" ? "Analytics cookies are on." : c === "denied" ? "Analytics cookies are off." : "You haven't chosen yet.";
    }
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-set]").forEach(function (b) {
      b.addEventListener("click", function () {
        var v = b.getAttribute("data-set");
        try {
          localStorage.setItem("consent", v);
        } catch (e) {}
        if (window.gtag) window.gtag("consent", "update", { analytics_storage: v });
        var banner = document.querySelector("[data-consent]");
        if (banner) banner.hidden = true;
        show();
      });
    });
    show();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 820px;
    padding-block: clamp(32px, 6vw, 72px);
  }
  .title {
    font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 80px);
    margin: 14px 0 28px;
    padding-bottom: 18px;
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .body {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 17.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .body p {
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }
  .body h2 {
    margin: 30px 0 8px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .body a {
    color: inherit;
  }
  .choice {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px 14px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .choice button {
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 650;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .choice button.ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
